\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {I}Introduction}{1}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The four interfaces trade robot-specific detail for abstraction and selective focus. The Joint-State Sequence{} serializes calibrated joint states; the Cartesian-Pose Sequence{} serializes link/EE poses and uses IK; the Symbolic Motion Program{} emits factorized \texttt  {pose} and \texttt  {path} symbols; and the Geometric Trajectory Sketch{} emits sparse EE/base-path handles retargeted by a controller. The latter two defer morphology grounding while preserving symbolic pose semantics or path geometry, respectively.}}{1}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:interfaces}{{1}{1}{}{}{}}
